# Task 162-028 Plan — CLI Advanced Commands READ-ONLY Audit

## Scope
READ-ONLY audit of `src/cli/commands/`:
- audit.ts
- feature-query.ts
- recover.ts
- docs.ts
- memory-query.ts (recall/remember UX)
- notify.ts
- metrics.ts

Output: ONE report at `docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-028-cli-advanced.md`

## Approach
1. Read each command file fully
2. Cross-reference with src/cli/index.ts (registration)
3. Apply 10 audit dimensions:
   1. Dead code (unused exports)
   2. ADR violations (focus ADR-010 single dep, ADR-012 register pattern, ADR-022-V2 CLI/MCP parity, ADR-011 readline)
   3. Conflicting areas (duplicated logic across commands)
   4. Drift (claims vs behavior, code comments vs reality)
   5. Type safety (any, ts-ignore, as unknown as)
   6. Dependency hygiene (.js extensions, circular deps)
   7. Documentation pollution
   8. Memory V2 coherence (especially memory-query.ts)
   9. Config integrity
   10. Migration triage (KEEP-PRIVATE | MIGRATE-PUBLIC | DELETE-CANDIDATE | UNCERTAIN)
4. Lead questions:
   - Sprint 150 new commands (audit, recover, docs) wired correctly?
   - Sprint 159 deckent metrics summary command quality?
   - recall/remember UX (memory-query.ts) — error handling, output format
5. Write report with mandatory format: Scope, Findings (P0/P1/P2/P3), Evidence (file:line), Migration triage, Recommendation

## Constraints
- READ-ONLY: NO source code edits
- Single output: docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-028-cli-advanced.md
- N/A for tests (read-only audit)
